# OpenSpec cycle

New features and behavior changes go through OpenSpec in this repo.

1. Unclear idea → `/opsx-explore` (no files, no code).
2. Known change → `/opsx-propose` (planning artifacts only; stop before coding).
3. Owner reviews **scenarios** for 2–5 minutes (not diffs).
4. `/opsx-apply` only after they accept the scenarios.
5. Give them the scenario checklist to test in the browser. Wait.
6. `/opsx-archive` after they confirm, or if they ask to archive.

Do not start implementing a behavior change until `openspec/changes/<name>/` exists, unless they say to skip OpenSpec. Tiny typo/build fixes may skip it.

The owner does not read code. After apply, do not paste large diffs. Point them at scenarios.

Existing `requirements/` docs are source material, not OpenSpec specs.
